==English==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|tea|room}}. In reference to a lavatory, probably as a variant of ''t-room'' ("[[toilet room]]").

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-tearoom.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[café]] which [[serve]]s [[tea]], [[usually]] with [[light]] [[food]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2019 November 6|title=Network News|journal=Rail|page=11|text=At [[Rannoch]], the platforms were rebuilt. Although the station '''tearoom''' couldn't be reached by rail during the closure, which started on October 5, it did help feed and sustain the workforce.}}
# {{label|en|euphemism|slang}} A [[public]] [[lavatory]], ''[[particularly]]'' {{label|en|US|_|gay|_|slang|dated}} as a [[meeting place]] for [[homosexual]] [[men]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1970|author=w:Laud Humphreys|title='''[[w:Tearoom Trade|Tearoom Trade]]'''}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1973|title=Deep Dick|chapter=ii|page=21
|passage=I'm deathly afraid of the [[tea room|tearoom]]s though, John. Some of my best friends have been entrapped and busted by the [[fuzz]].}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1975|title=Hard-Headed Dick|chapter=iii|page=39
|passage=I had run into Grant in a [[tea room|tea-room]]—The busy main floor [[crapper]]—a few months earlier.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2014|title=[https://books.google.co.jp/books?id=bHytBAAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover A Cultural Encyclopedia of the Penis]|pageurl=https://books.google.co.jp/books?id=bHytBAAAQBAJ&pg=PA216|page=216
|passage=The euphemistically named "[[tea room]]" has been used in sexual subcultures among men who have sex with men (MSM) to describe public sex environments, usually public toilets, where men meet other men in sexual interaction... The term itself might be outdated...}}
# {{lb|en|Australia}} A [[room]] in a [[workplace]] [[set aside]] for [[tea break]]s, [[lunch break]]s, [[snack]]ing, etc.; a [[break room]].

